  "full_text": "There's a story about The Rock, the Jewish bodybuilder, wearing shirts that are two sizes too small. This is fat clothes. What should I do about fat clothes? Fucking figuratively, because more fat clothes in your ass. It's like fucking perfect justice and you use too much toilet paper. You want to use the right amount. That's what you want to use. Clean and unclean. Do you know? Is there any blessing in living in the luxury of clean? What if, like, he didn't have the luxury of clean? Do we have the... Imagine in Bible times, it was a much more visceral concept of clean. Anyway, so, like, the governing guilt. Am I clean? Am I unclean? Has that circuit been taken offline? And how many forms of clean are there? Like a pure mind or a sullied mind? And we were talking about falls from grace and maybe the highest life form is the one that has the greatest dynamic range in falls from grace. What? So like if you can look both ugly and attractive, get a dynamic range of grace. What?",
